# REPLACE THE VALUES BELOW WITH YOUR ACTUAL KEYS IF NOT AUTOMATICALLY SET

# These are placeholder values, not a real project — Google sign-in
# (AccountSection.tsx) and Firestore (user profiles + recent routes, see
# src/lib/firebase/*) stay in a clean "not configured yet" state until real
# values are set here. To enable it:
#   1. Firebase Console (console.firebase.google.com) > your project >
#      Project settings (gear icon) > General tab > "Your apps" > the Web
#      app named "Tesla Map Web" (Add app > Web if it doesn't exist yet).
#   2. Copy the six values from its `firebaseConfig` object into the six
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* values below (all safe to expose client-side —
#      Firebase's web config is not a secret; access is controlled by
#      Firestore/Auth security rules, not by hiding these values).
#   3. Authentication > Sign-in method > enable the "Google" provider.
#   4. Authentication > Settings > Authorized domains — add BOTH:
#        localhost
#        geonav-red.vercel.app
#      (Firebase redirects back to whatever origin initiated sign-in, so
#      both dev and the current production domain need to be allow-listed.)
#   5. Firestore Database > Create database (production mode) if you
#      haven't already, then add security rules so each user can only read
#      /write their own users/{uid} document, e.g.:
#        match /users/{uid} { allow read, write: if request.auth.uid == uid; }
